▶ P03-C Host consumer · governed read on the production service path
  ✔ admission → create intent → binding → root turn → claim → governed repo_read → retained bytes → one submission → root terminal → later input on the same binding (1215.45075ms)
  ✔ unadvertised, wrong-turn, malformed and out-of-scope calls read nothing; each refusal is retained and delivered once as an error (1440.920917ms)
  ✔ policy deny and a user's deny never read; a scope revoked while approval is pending cancels the run unread, and a later run has no reader (2005.998292ms)
  ✔ a native call observed twice is claimed once, executed once and submitted once; racing claims share one receipt (1095.865625ms)
  ✔ without attributable root identity nothing is read and nothing settles the run; a required action is not root evidence (455.379833ms)
  ✔ a lost creation reply stays unknown: no binding, no guessed id, no replacement session, and the chat is fenced (944.925833ms)
  ✔ a lost submission reply keeps the retained result and its identity: unknown delivery, no re-read, no re-send, chat fenced (1058.557959ms)
  ✔ restart fences: an interrupted execution and an unanswered submission become unknown; nothing is re-read, re-run or re-sent (1141.180416ms)
  ✔ an earlier stream replayed to a later run cannot re-execute, re-associate or settle it (793.277708ms)
  ✔ a chat stays with its runtime: Pi refuses a remote-bound chat, the remote runtime refuses a Pi chat, and a changed configuration cannot reuse the binding (938.109083ms)
✔ P03-C Host consumer · governed read on the production service path (11090.902916ms)
▶ P03-D · cancellation
  ✔ cancel is an intent; the root turn ending cancelled confirms it, the retained result is not delivered, and the chat continues (1632.1985ms)
  ✔ an accepted cancel that is never confirmed gets one last turn read, then stays unknown and fences the chat until the turn is seen to end (1000.19725ms)
  ✔ a cancel whose reply is lost, or that is refused, is sent once and leaves the run unknown (1514.974208ms)
